\section{Limitations}
\label{sec:vfour-10}

The evaluation fixes UAV assignments and mission sequences. Core-72 uses repeated controlled constructions with synthetic discrete parameters. The network experiments cover twelve compact synthetic networks with three paired disruptions each; a shared hub creates the service-capacity shortage, and the resulting repairs primarily adjust departures and charging. Reassignment, more varied demand and larger spatial networks may require different forms of coordination.

The network flight model represents one empirically parameterized aircraft operating at constant phase speeds without wind. Charging parameters are scenario assumptions, and ground-wait consumption, weather uncertainty and detailed aircraft separation are outside the model. Each model generates one response per task; preference sensitivity uses a fixed Core candidate pool, and network local search permits four mission changes within a 600-s budget. Repeated generation and broader search budgets would help establish how consistently the observed complementarity persists.

